<h1>HUD API</h1>
<p>HUD stands for heads-up display: the on-screen interface layer — health bars, score, menus, touch buttons. In DemiEngine the HUD is an authored document of named nodes that scripts can find, update, animate, and query for tests.</p>

<h2>What a HUD node is</h2>
<p>A HUD is a tree of nodes (labels, bars, buttons, panels). Every node has a stable ID from the authored document, so scripts address nodes by name instead of hunting through a hierarchy. The <code>demi.hud</code> module is how a script finds a node and changes what the player sees.</p>
<pre><code>local Hud = require("demi.hud")

local bar = Hud.find("skyforge_health_bar")   -- node handle, or nil if the ID is unknown</code></pre>
<p><code>Hud.find(id)</code> returns a generation-checked handle, or <code>nil</code> when the ID is missing. Structural operations and tweens use handles; content and state setters use ID strings.</p>

<h2>Creating and structuring nodes</h2>
<pre><code>local Hud = require("demi.hud")

local row, err = Hud.create("skyforge_menu", {
    type = "panel",
    id = "skyforge_row_1",
    text = "Continue",
    width = 240, height = 48,
})
if not row then print(err) end

if row then
    local copy, clone_err = Hud.clone(row, "skyforge_row_2")
    if copy then Hud.reparent(copy, "skyforge_other_panel") end
end
local kids = Hud.children("skyforge_menu")  -- array of child IDs
Hud.clear_children("skyforge_menu")          -- invalidates handles to its children</code></pre>
<ul>
  <li><code>Hud.create(parent_id, def)</code> — atomically creates a native subtree or UI-prefab instance. It accepts HUD layout fields, nested <code>children</code>, colors and target-based <code>overrides</code>. Returns a root handle or <code>nil</code>, plus an error string. Older <code>x</code>/<code>y</code>/<code>width</code>/<code>height</code> fields remain available for native node definitions.</li>
  <li><code>Hud.apply_action(name)</code> — applies declared show/hide/focus effects and relayouts the HUD. Returns whether the action exists; prefab-local names are qualified with the instance ID.</li>
  <li><code>Hud.clone(source_handle, new_root_id, parent_id?)</code> — copies a subtree. Returns handle or <code>nil</code>, plus an error string.</li>
  <li><code>Hud.remove(handle)</code> — deletes a node and its subtree. Returns success boolean plus an error string.</li>
  <li><code>Hud.reparent(handle, parent_id)</code> — moves a node. Returns success boolean plus an error string.</li>
  <li><code>Hud.clear_children(parent_id)</code> — removes all children. Returns success boolean plus an error string.</li>
  <li><code>Hud.children(parent_id)</code> — returns an array of child ID strings.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Content and appearance</h2>
<pre><code>local Hud = require("demi.hud")

Hud.set_text("skyforge_score", "0")
print(Hud.get_text("skyforge_score"))    -- "0"

Hud.set_font("skyforge_score", "asset://fonts/skyforge_ui")
Hud.set_font_size("skyforge_score", 18)
Hud.set_color("skyforge_score", 1, 1, 1, 1)
Hud.set_background_color("skyforge_score", 0, 0, 0, 0.5)
Hud.set_image("skyforge_portrait", "asset://textures/skyforge_ace", 0, 0, 256, 256)
Hud.set_opacity("skyforge_score", 0.8)</code></pre>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Call</th><th>Takes</th><th>Returns</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>Hud.set_text(id, text)</code></td><td>ID string, text string</td><td>boolean</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Hud.get_text(id)</code></td><td>ID string</td><td>String, or <code>nil</code> when the node is missing</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Hud.set_font(id, uri)</code></td><td>ID string, <code>asset://</code> font URI or empty string for fallback</td><td>boolean</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Hud.set_font_size(id, size)</code></td><td>ID string, number in canvas units</td><td>boolean</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Hud.set_color(id, r, g, b, a?)</code></td><td>ID string, 0…1 color components</td><td>boolean</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Hud.set_background_color(id, r, g, b, a?)</code></td><td>ID string, 0…1 color components</td><td>boolean</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Hud.set_image(id, uri, x, y, w, h)</code></td><td>ID string, texture URI, source rectangle</td><td>boolean</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Hud.set_opacity(id, alpha)</code></td><td>ID string, number 0…1</td><td>boolean</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p>Lua color setters take separate red, green, blue, and optional alpha numbers from 0 to 1. JSON color fields can use arrays or hex strings. Sizes and positions use HUD canvas units.</p>
<pre><code>Hud.set_value("skyforge_health_bar", 0.75)   -- progress-style nodes: 0…1 (or the node's range)
Hud.set_checked("skyforge_mute_toggle", true)
Hud.set_disabled("skyforge_play_button", true)
Hud.set_visible("skyforge_warning", false)
Hud.set_position("skyforge_banner", 40, 12)
Hud.set_size("skyforge_banner", 200, 48)</code></pre>
<ul>
  <li><code>Hud.set_value(id, number)</code> — fills sliders and progress bars. Returns a success boolean.</li>
  <li><code>Hud.set_checked(node, boolean)</code> — checkbox/toggle state.</li>
  <li><code>Hud.set_disabled(node, boolean)</code> — blocks interaction and can grey out the look.</li>
  <li><code>Hud.set_visible(node, boolean)</code> — shows or hides without destroying the node.</li>
  <li><code>Hud.set_position(id, x, y)</code> / <code>Hud.set_size(id, w, h)</code> — canvas-unit layout overrides. Return success booleans.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Focus</h2>
<pre><code>Hud.focus_next()
print(Hud.focused())    -- focused node ID string, or "" when nothing has focus</code></pre>
<p><code>Hud.focus_next(reverse?)</code> moves keyboard/controller focus and returns whether it succeeded. <code>Hud.focused()</code> returns the focused node's ID string, or an empty string when nothing has focus.</p>

<h2>Variables and localization</h2>
<p>Variables are named values that text nodes can interpolate, so one script write updates every label bound to that name.</p>
<pre><code>local Hud = require("demi.hud")

Hud.set_variable("score", "1200")
Hud.set_variables({ wave = "3", lives = "2" })
print(Hud.has_variable("score"))       -- true
print(Hud.get_variable("score"))       -- "1200", or nil when unset

Hud.reset_variables()                  -- clear runtime values

Hud.set_locale("de")
Hud.set_pseudo_locale(true)            -- stretch text to spot overflow</code></pre>
<ul>
  <li><code>Hud.set_variable(name, value)</code> / <code>Hud.set_variables(table)</code> — assign declared names to string values. Return a success boolean plus an error string.</li>
  <li><code>Hud.has_variable(name)</code> → boolean.</li>
  <li><code>Hud.get_variable(name)</code> → the value, or <code>nil</code> when unset.</li>
  <li><code>Hud.reset_variables()</code> — clears runtime values; unresolved markers remain visible.</li>
  <li><code>Hud.set_locale(tag)</code> — selects a locale in the loaded HUD's <code>locales</code> object; returns a boolean and error string. <code>Hud.set_pseudo_locale(on)</code> changes presentation without a return value.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Tweens and motion</h2>
<p>A tween animates one property over time. Supported properties: <code>opacity</code>, <code>x</code>, <code>y</code>, <code>scale</code>.</p>
<pre><code>local Hud = require("demi.hud")

local banner = Hud.find("skyforge_banner")
local handle, err = Hud.tween(banner, "opacity", 0, 0.35)
if not handle then print(err) end

Hud.cancel_tween(handle)          -- stop mid-flight; returns true when cancelled
Hud.set_reduced_motion(true)      -- honour accessibility preference</code></pre>
<ul>
  <li><code>Hud.tween(handle, property, target, duration)</code> → tween ID and error string. Animates <code>opacity</code>, <code>x</code>, <code>y</code>, or <code>scale</code> toward <code>target</code> over <code>duration</code> seconds. Tweens cancel themselves when the node is removed.</li>
  <li><code>Hud.cancel_tween(handle)</code> → boolean.</li>
  <li><code>Hud.set_reduced_motion(enabled)</code> — finishes presentation changes immediately for players who prefer fewer animations.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Virtualized lists</h2>
<p>Long lists (a Skyforge server browser with hundreds of rows) should only build the rows on screen. Virtualization helpers report which rows are visible and recycle off-screen ones.</p>
<pre><code>local Hud = require("demi.hud")

-- Which rows are on screen right now?
local first, count = Hud.visible_range(500, 44, scroll_offset, viewport_height)
-- first: one-based index of the first visible row
-- count: how many live rows the viewport needs

-- How tall is the whole list, and which rows fill it?
local layout, err = Hud.virtual_layout(row_extents)  -- row_extents: array of numbers
if layout then
    -- layout fields per the HudVirtualLayout stub
end

-- Reuse hidden template rows for stable keys:
local rows = Hud.recycle_rows("skyforge_server_list", row_template, keys, extents, scroll_offset, viewport_height)
-- rows: array of { key, index, node, offset, extent, rebound }</code></pre>
<ul>
  <li><code>Hud.visible_range(item_count, item_extent, scroll_offset, viewport_extent, overscan?)</code> → <code>integer first, integer count</code>. One-based logical index of the first visible row and how many live rows the screen needs.</li>
  <li><code>Hud.virtual_layout(item_extents)</code> → <code>layout, error</code> — planning helper over per-row extents.</li>
  <li><code>Hud.recycle_rows(collection_id, row_template, keys, extents, scroll_offset, viewport_extent)</code> → recycled rows with <code>key</code>, <code>index</code>, a live <code>node</code> handle, <code>offset</code>, <code>extent</code>, and <code>rebound</code> (true when the pool slot was reset for a new key).</li>
</ul>

<h2>Accessibility snapshot</h2>
<pre><code>local nodes = Hud.accessibility_snapshot()
-- nodes: array of accessibility nodes (possibly empty, never nil)</code></pre>
<p><code>Hud.accessibility_snapshot()</code> takes no arguments and describes the whole active document. Each entry carries <code>id</code>, <code>parent</code>, <code>role</code> (for example <code>button</code>, <code>slider</code>, <code>static_text</code>), <code>label</code>, <code>description</code>, numeric <code>value</code>/<code>minimum</code>/<code>maximum</code> plus display <code>value_text</code>, position and size (<code>x</code>, <code>y</code>, <code>width</code>, <code>height</code>), and state booleans (<code>focused</code>, <code>disabled</code>, <code>checked</code>, <code>focusable</code>, <code>offscreen</code>). The array is empty when nothing is announced — never <code>nil</code>.</p>

